{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-conjugate-radius-bound","title":"thm:pet-ch6-conjugate-radius-bound","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":602,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#thm:pet-ch6-conjugate-radius-bound","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#ex:pet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-hessian-r]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch6-conjugate-radius-bound","line":1358,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[conjugate-radius comparison]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch6-conjugate-radius-bound}\n\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0273}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison, ex:pet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form}\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.4.6}\n  If $(M,g)$ has $\\sec\\le K$, $K>0$, then\n  $\\exp_p:B(0,\\pi/\\sqrt K)\\to M$ has no critical points.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison, rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-hessian-r}\n  \\sketch\n  Rauch comparison makes \\(|J(t)|/\\operatorname{sn}_K(t)\\) nondecreasing with positive limit \\(|\\dot J(0)|\\) at \\(0\\). Therefore no nontrivial \\(J\\) vanishes before \\(\\pi/\\sqrt K\\), so \\(D\\exp_p\\) is nonsingular there.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[conjugate-radius comparison] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d636f6e6a75676174652d7261646975732d626f756e64\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0273</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-rauch-comparison\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23ex%3Apet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form\">↗ ex:pet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:6.4.6</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sec \\le K$\">$\\sec \\le K$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K&gt;0$\">$K&gt;0$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p:B(0,\\pi /\\sqrt K)\\to M$\">$\\exp _p:B(0,\\pi /\\sqrt K)\\to M$</span> has no critical points.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-rauch-comparison\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23rem%3Apet-ch6-jacobi-hessian-r\">↗ rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-hessian-r</a> \\sketch Rauch comparison makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|J(t)|/\\operatorname {sn}_K(t)$\">$|J(t)|/\\operatorname {sn}_K(t)$</span> nondecreasing with positive limit <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\dot J(0)|$\">$|\\dot J(0)|$</span> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0$\">$0$</span>. Therefore no nontrivial <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J$\">$J$</span> vanishes before <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi /\\sqrt K$\">$\\pi /\\sqrt K$</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$D\\exp _p$\">$D\\exp _p$</span> is nonsingular there. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#ex:pet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-injectivity-radius-nonpositive","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison","title":"thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison","label":"thm:pet-ch6-rauch-comparison"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#ex:pet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form","title":"ex:pet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form","label":"ex:pet-ch6-conjugate-point-space-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-hessian-r","title":"rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-hessian-r","label":"rem:pet-ch6-jacobi-hessian-r"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-klingenberg-injectivity-estimate","title":"lem:pet-ch6-klingenberg-injectivity-estimate","label":"lem:pet-ch6-klingenberg-injectivity-estimate"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-ex-6-7-4","title":"rem:pet-ch6-ex-6-7-4","label":"rem:pet-ch6-ex-6-7-4"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-conjugate-radius-bou